5116|# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- task lock + pending record
5117|#
5118|# OWNERSHIP and RECOVERY METADATA are two different files:
5119|#
5120|#   <task>/.consult.lock          ownership. A PERMANENT file at a stable path: opened
5121|#                                 with FileMode.OpenOrCreate and held open for the whole
5122|#                                 critical section; release = close the handle, never
5123|#                                 unlink (a contender that already opened the path must
5124|#                                 never end up locking a different file than the next
5125|#                                 one). The OS decides ownership: a holder that dies
5126|#                                 loses it with its handle. Share mode:
5127|#                                   * Windows: FileShare.Read - a refused contender can
5128|#                                     read the holder's record for its message, nobody
5129|#                                     else can open it for writing;
5130|#                                   * elsewhere: FileShare.None, which .NET on Unix
5131|#                                     emulates with an advisory flock(LOCK_EX) (any other
5132|#                                     share mode maps to a shared lock that would not
5133|#                                     exclude).
5134|#                                 Cross-host exclusion (a task directory on a network
5135|#                                 share used from two machines) is out of scope. The
5136|#                                 content is informational only - { pid, start_time,
5137|#                                 host, task, started } of the current holder, plus
5138|#                                 `panel` (its id) while a -Panel run holds it - written
5139|#                                 after the handle is held; overwriting it destroys
5140|#                                 nothing recoverable. A -Panel run holds it for the
5141|#                                 whole panel; its members never take it.
5142|#
5143|#   <task>/.consult.write.lock    (0.4.x wave 21) the COMMIT lock of the task's two stores,
5144|#                                 same discipline (permanent file, held open, release =
5145|#                                 close, a killed holder releases it), held only for one
